\title{09 · Bibliography and proof routes — revision 1}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/09-bibliography.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{These references supply definitions and comparison routes. A source about ordinary VDCs, Segal categories, or a different model does not prove the corresponding theorem for the candidate augmented ∞-root. The full original annotated bibliography is preserved in \code{history/v0/09-bibliography.md}; the active routes and their limits follow.}
\table{
  \tr{\th{Primary source}\th{What is used}\th{Boundary of the claim}}
  \tr{\td{Koudenburg, [Augmented virtual double categories](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.11189), published TAC 2020; arXiv v4 includes later corrections}\td{Exact discrete augmentation, restrictions, units, vertical cells, and equivalence comparison for \ref{dec-kr-0018}, \ref{dec-rt-0021}, \ref{dec-ft-0006}}\td{The augmented ∞-arity/model construction is new work. Pin the version used when transcribing axioms.}}
  \tr{\td{Cruttwell–Shulman, [A unified framework for generalized multicategories](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0907.2460)}\td{Discrete Mod/Kleisli definitions and scoped preservation results}\td{Examples 3.12–3.14 distinguish list monads on matrices from symmetric/braided monoidal category monads on profunctors. No ∞-preservation theorem is inferred by changing the word “category.”}}
  \tr{\td{Berger–Melliès–Weber, [Monads with arities and their associated theories](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1101.3064)}\td{General nerve recognition; separately, canonical arity results under stronger hypotheses}\td{\ref{dec-kr-0015}/04 record actual hypotheses for arities, generic factorization, and the chosen elementary cores. Reedy structure is additional.}}
  \tr{\td{Bergner, [Complete Segal spaces arising from simplicial categories](https://arxiv.org/html/0704.1624v2)}\td{Distinguish strict/relative diagram maps from categorical presentations; ordinary-category comparisons in \ref{at-fd-0004}}\td{Reedy replacement and categorical completion have different roles. This is not a construction of the candidate VDC∞ localization.}}
  \tr{\td{Lean, [Definitions reference](https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Definitions/Definitions/)}\td{Opaque declarations and specification packaging for \ref{dec-rt-0028}}\td{Prototype against the pinned Lean version. An opaque body alone does not export implementation-specific laws.}}
  \tr{\td{Lean, [Validating a Lean Proof](https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/ValidatingProofs/)}\td{Dependency and axiom inspection for \ref{dec-tl-0017}}\td{A stub build checks clients under assumptions; the matching implementation and axiom audit are still required.}}
}
